title: Famine Relief
subtitle: The 1921 relief committee.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: soviet_affairs
view-if: fiscal_policy_timer <= 0 and dix >= 108 and famine_relief = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; fiscal_policy_timer = 2

The Volga is starving. Maxim Gorky has proposed a committee of public figures, including socialists and Kadets, to collect relief at home and abroad. The government has agreed to allow it, for the moment.

- @join: Join the committee, and send our members to work for it.
- @decline: Leave it to the government.
- @easy_discard

@join
on-arrival: {!
Q.famine_relief = 1;
RO.add(Q, {bread: 3, repression: 3, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 4, peasants: 5, middle: 5});
RO.fac(Q, 'unions', 2, -2);
if (Q.foreign_pressure >= 1) { Q.foreign_pressure += 1; }
!}

The committee began collecting money and grain. It is the first time since 1917 that Kadets, socialists and engineers have worked together. It cannot last.

@decline
on-arrival: {!
Q.famine_relief = 2;
RO.boost(Q, {peasants: -3, middle: -3});
RO.add(Q, {repression: -1});
!}

We declined to join, and said we would not cooperate with a regime that was not free. Several of our members signed up as individuals.
